      "id": "r2",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "existence, when shall we, loudly uttering the words “S'iva,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "S'iva” have our eyes flooded with copious tears proceeding",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "from supreme bliss !",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "87. Having given away every thing with a heart full of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "tender compassion, and remembering the courses of destiny",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "having adverse ends in this wordly existence, (when) shall",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "we pass, in a sacred forest, the nights lit with the rays of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "full autumnal moon, the feet of Hara being the sole refuge",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "of our mind !",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "88. When shall I, wearing a small strip of cloth, and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "residing in Vârânasî ( Benares ) on the bank of the river",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "of gods pass my days like a moment crying out “ Have",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "mercy, oh Lord of Gaurî, Destroyer of the Three Cities,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "oh S'ambhu, oh Three-eyed God,” having placed on my",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "head my folded palms !",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "89. Having bathed in the waters of the Ganges, and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "worshipped Thee, O Lord, with fruits and flowers undefiled,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "and having fixed my attention, sitting on a stony couch in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "the gorge of a mountain, on thee, the object of contemplation,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "when shall I, O Enemy of Smara, be free by Thy grace,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "from the pain of serving a master having hands and feet",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "just like myself, delightfully carrying out the words of the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "preceptor, living on fruits ( only ) and self-complacent.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "90. O S'ambhu, when shall I, living all alone, free from",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "desire and peaceful, and having for my pot my hand ( only )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "and for my garments the quarters, be able to root out Karma?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "91. A certain path ( i. e. of Moksha ), easily attainable",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "by the favour of Shiva, opens up for the yogins, who use the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "hand as a pot, who are contented with alms which are intrin-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "sically pure, who sit any where, who ever look upon the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "world as almost like grass and who have all acquired, even",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "without casting off the body, the knowledge of the uninter-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "rupted and supreme delight ( of Brahman ).",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    }
  ],
